.TH "SCCFM-CLI INVENTORY DEVICES FTD UPGRADE TRIGGER" "1" "2026-08-26" "0.40.0" "sccfm-cli inventory devices ftd upgrade trigger Manual"
.SH NAME
sccfm-cli\-inventory\-devices\-ftd\-upgrade\-trigger \- Trigger an FTD firmware upgrade on one or...
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sccfm-cli inventory devices ftd upgrade trigger
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Trigger an FTD firmware upgrade on one or more devices. Supports staging (download + readiness check only) or full upgrade.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-device\-name TEXT
Device name to search for (supports wildcards like 'branch-*').
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-query TEXT
Filter devices by a Lucene query.
.TP
\fB\-l,\fP \-\-limit INTEGER RANGE
Maximum records to return  [default: 50; 1<=x<=200]
.TP
\fB\-o,\fP \-\-offset INTEGER RANGE
Pagination offset  [default: 0; x>=0]
.TP
\fB\-u,\fP \-\-device\-uids TEXT
List of device UIDs to upgrade.
.TP
\fB\-\-software\-version\fP TEXT
Target FTD software version (e.g. '7.4.1').  [required]
.TP
\fB\-\-stage\-upgrade\fP
Stage the upgrade only (download image + readiness checks). The upgrade will NOT be applied to the device.
.TP
\fB\-\-ignore\-maintenance\-window\fP
Allow upgrade even if the device is outside its maintenance window.
.TP
\fB\-\-upgrade\-name\fP TEXT
Human-readable name to identify and track the upgrade run.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Run a preflight check without performing the operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fP / \-\-no\-wait
Wait for the transaction to finish before returning.  [default: no-wait]
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fP INTEGER RANGE
Maximum seconds to wait for the transaction to complete (used with --wait).  [default: 3600; x>=1]
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP [table|json]
Output format  [default: table]
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-path\fP PATH
Path to the configuration file (defaults to ~/.sccfm-cli/config.json).
